      {
        "id": 225388,
        "name": "Phantom5613",
        "username": "Phantom5613",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/{size}/1906_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-02-27T04:38:53.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"davethegame\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/davethegame/48/2051_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> davethegame:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>There’s an archetype called “Modular” that covers heroes like Bunker and Muerto. It’s… complicated. But the text under Modular walks you through the whole thing step-by-step.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Say I wanted to make a size-altering hero, not that different from the likes of Sky Screper or A*t-Man. Would the Modular archetype be the one I should consider to build that kind of character?</p>",
        "post_number": 125,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:59:00.675Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
