      {
        "id": 225397,
        "name": "rickjonzz",
        "username": "rickjonzz",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rickjonzz/{size}/1934_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-03-12T15:14:04.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Rabit\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/48/5774_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Rabit:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Some folks want the character generation chapter early. I believe that’s what they are asking about.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Hey, I wouldn’t say no to the Villain and Environment generation chapters either.&nbsp; ;-)&nbsp;</p>\n<p>But seriously, yeah, many of us have&nbsp;been itching to play this game since the Starter Kit. And some companies give advance looks at books to backers - things like plaintext versions of the rules. No art. Sometimes barely any formatting.&nbsp;But there’s also plenty of companies that, like GTG, don’t show backers anything until it’s practically done - where there’s just enough wiggle room to fix glaring errors. And I’ve done enough freelancing in the RPG industry to see both sides of the arguement.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>So as much as I was hoping that as soon GTG got the cash from kickstarter that we’d get copies of whatever it was they were using in the livesteams, I was also steeling myself to the idea that we wouldn’t see anything until around August.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 134,
        "post_type": 1,
